of inspection, home energy systems, solar heat pumps, home battery installation, EV charger installation, insulation & sealing, solar shade installation -> /, /services", "25-year performance guarantee -> /, /about-us", "Fully licensed and insured -> /", "Free home solar assessment and custom system design -> /, /services", "Financing options available -> /", "25 million kWh clean solar energy produced -> /", "Over 2,000 tons CO2 eliminated annually -> /", "33,000 trees worth of annual carbon capture -> /", "Physical installation 1-2 days; full process 4-8 weeks -> /", "Panels last 25-30 years with 80% output guarantee -> /", "Roof condition assessed before solar installation -> /", "Local knowledge of NC climate, utility infrastructure, permits, incentives -> /about-us", "Values: honesty, quality, sustainability, accountability -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are a locally owned and operated solar installation and roofing company serving homeowners across North Carolina.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='spi-solar-panel-installation-nc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SRS Fabrication Inc. was established in 2005 in North Las Vegas, Nevada. The company began as a modest 5,000-square-foot facility and has since grown into a multi-building operation spanning over 56,000 square feet of production space.

The shop provides a full range of custom fabrication services, including precision welding and fabrication, sheet metal work, CNC machining, tube and plate bending, waterjet cutting, and manual milling. Its carpentry department operates CNC routers for wood, composites, and solid-surface materials, while the artistic division runs a 4-axis CNC foam carving router, a hard-coat finishing system, and a thermoforming station for plastics. In-house drafting and design supports 3D modeling, photorealistic rendering, finite-element analysis, and CNC programming. The staff includes certified welders, project managers, draftsmen, carpenters, and scenic sculptors and painters.

Customers include clients seeking creative structural displays, architectural pieces, and custom scenic elements.

