UPDATE companies SET description='Sag Harbor Industries, Inc. was founded in 1946 by Charles Edison, son of inventor Thomas Edison, in the village of Sag Harbor, New York. The company began with a single goal: to manufacture electrical coils and inductors of superior quality. Today it operates from two U.S. manufacturing locations — its original headquarters in Sag Harbor, NY, and a second facility in Farmville, North Carolina.

The company produces custom power, control, and instrumentation transformers and coils, along with cable assemblies, printed circuit board assemblies, and full box-build integration. Its coil portfolio spans electric, encapsulated, field, molded, self-supported, solenoid, varnished, and toroidal types, manufactured through winding, injection molding, transfer molding, and vacuum impregnation processes. The facilities are equipped with automated and semi-automated equipment geared for high-volume, medium-volume, and short-run production.

Sag Harbor serves electronics, aerospace, medical device, renewable energy, industrial automation, and automotive sectors. Aerospace customers receive UL-compliant components built to AS9100 standards; medical device makers rely on ISO 13485-certified, burr-free coils for implants and diagnostic equipment; renewable energy projects use toroidal coils and transformers for solar and wind systems; and automation firms source durable solenoid coils and cable assemblies for robotics and machinery.

The founder''s original mandate — superior quality — remains the stated differentiator. The company emphasizes 100% U.S. manufacturing, engineering and design competence, flexible supply chain management, and on-time delivery. It holds ISO 9001:2015, AS9100, and ISO 13485 certifications, and its products meet UL insulation system standards.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100','ISO 13485']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom coil winding (electric, encapsulated, field, molded, self-supported, solenoid, varnished, toroidal)", "Power, control, and instrumentation transformer manufacturing", "Cable assembly", "Printed circuit board assembly", "Box build assembly", "Injection molding", "Transfer molding", "Vacuum impregnation", "UL insulation system compliance", "Design consultation and engineering support"], "industries": ["Electronics", "Aerospace", "Medical devices", "Renewable energy", "Industrial automation", "Automotive"], "materials": ["Copper magnet wire"], "equipment": [], "volume": "High volume, medium volume, and short run production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1946 by Charles Edison (son of Thomas Edison) -> db, /", "Headquarters Sag Harbor, NY; second facility Farmville, NC -> /", "Products: custom power/control/instrumentation transformers, coils, cable assemblies, PCB & box build -> /", "Coil types: electric, encapsulated, field, molded, self-supported, solenoid, varnished, toroidal -> /", "Processes: winding, injection molding, transfer molding, vacuum impregnation -> /", "Volume: high, medium, short run production -> /", "Industries served: electronics, aerospace, medical, renewable energy, industrial automation, automotive -> /", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, AS9100, ISO 13485, UL standards -> /, db", "100% Made in USA manufacturer -> /", "Engineering & design competence, flexible supply chain, on-time delivery -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom power, control, and instrumentation transformers/coils (founded 1946 by Charles Edison)", "founded_year": "1946", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/sag-harbor-industries/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sag-harbor-industries-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sage Plastics, Inc. operates from its headquarters in Fort Worth, Texas, with manufacturing facilities in Long Beach and Colton, California. The company traces its roots to a blow molding plant established in Long Beach over 18 years ago, which remains the longest-tenured site in its network. In 2022, the company opened a greenfield facility in Fort Worth to serve the Midwest and Southeast, and in 2023 it acquired Microdyne''s Colton operation, adding injection molding to its blow molding capabilities.

The company specializes in blow molding and injection molding of high-density polyethylene (HDPE) bottles and containers for dairy, beverage, foodservice, industrial, chemical, and household markets. Its Long Beach plant focuses on core product lines for industrial/chemical and foodservice segments, while the Colton facility offers both injection and blow molding with extensive customization. The Fort Worth site was built as a versatile manufacturing hub.

Sage Plastics serves customers in the dairy, beverage, foodservice, industrial, chemical, and household sectors, providing both standard and custom containers. The company emphasizes food safety certification and uses statistical quality control (SPC) methods across its operations.

The company differentiates itself through speed-to-market capabilities, a logistics department designed to handle any shipping requirement, and a quality system that includes special testing methods and SPC. It aims to be the preferred supplier of plastic containers by combining service, quality, and execution.', certifications=ARRAY['IMS','ISO','Food safety certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Blow molding", "Injection molding", "Custom molding", "Statistical Quality Control (SPC)", "Special testing methods", "Logistics and shipping", "Food safety compliance"], "industries": ["Dairy", "Beverage", "Foodservice", "Industrial", "Chemical", "Household"], "materials": ["HDPE (high-density polyethylene)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Speed-to-market capabilities", "Logistics department capable of handling any shipping need", "Statistical Quality Control (SPC) methods", "Food safety certification", "IMS and ISO certified facilities", "Combined injection and blow molding at Colton facility"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Fort Worth, Texas -> /", "Long Beach plant established over 18 years ago -> /", "Colton facility added in 2023 with injection and blow molding -> /", "Fort Worth greenfield facility opened in 2022 -> /", "Manufactures HDPE bottles via blow molding and injection molding -> /", "Serves dairy, beverage, foodservice, industrial, chemical, household markets -> /", "IMS and ISO certified facilities -> /", "Food safety certification and SPC methods -> /", "Speed-to-market and logistics capabilities -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "A leading manufacturer of high-quality HDPE bottles for a wide range of industries and applications", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sage-plastics' AND 