UPDATE companies SET description='Savannah Food Company, based in Savannah, Tennessee, traces its roots to 1970 when Bob Hagy, after decades in the restaurant business, began producing hushpuppies using family recipes. The Catfish Hotel Restaurant, still operating today, had built a reputation for its freshly made hushpuppies, prompting Hagy to build a dedicated processing facility. In 2004, the company was acquired by John Bryan, whose family had founded Bryan Foods, Inc. in the early 1900s.

The company operates a food processing facility that manufactures hushpuppies and side dishes, including original, jalapeño, and sweet corn varieties. Its quality system incorporates a hazard analysis and critical control points (HACCP) plan, good manufacturing practices (GMP), and alignment with global food safety initiatives (GFSI). The facility has held FSSC 22000 certification since June 2013, a globally recognized food safety standard based on ISO principles.

Savannah Food Company supplies wholesome, easy-to-prepare hushpuppies and side dishes to customers seeking authentic Southern recipes. Its products are positioned as comparable to scratch-made family meals.

The business emphasizes food safety and quality as the responsibility of every employee, backed by preventive control management, continuous improvement, and the FSSC 22000 certification. The original processing facility was built to replicate the restaurant-quality hushpuppies that made the Catfish Hotel famous.', certifications=ARRAY['FSSC 22000']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Food processing", "Hushpuppy production", "Side dish production", "HACCP-based food safety management", "GMP compliance", "GFSI compliance", "FSSC 22000 certified operations"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["FSSC 22000 certified facility since June 2013", "HACCP, GMP, and GFSI compliance", "Authentic Southern family recipes", "Processing facility built to replicate restaurant-quality hushpuppies"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1970 by Bob Hagy -> /about", "Purchased by John Bryan in 2004 -> /about", "FSSC 22000 certification since June 2013 -> /about", "HACCP, GMP, GFSI compliance -> /about", "Produces hushpuppies and side dishes from authentic Southern recipes -> /", "Processing facility built to replicate restaurant-quality hushpuppies -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Savannah Food Company has been in the food processing business since 1970 when Bob Hagy started making hushpuppies", "founded_year": "1970", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='savannah-food-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Saw Logs to Lumber operates from a Boschertown building on North Highway 94 in St. Charles, Missouri. The company traces its start to 1994, when Wayne, a Vietnam War veteran and former Boeing technical representative, purchased the floodplain property after recognizing its highway visibility and proximity to his then-employer. Wayne’s woodworking roots reach back to age 13, when a neighbor’s unpaid debt led him to acquire a table saw and lumber, with which he built a boat and dock.

The shop runs two sawmills and maintains an inventory exceeding 50,000 board feet of live-edge slabs alongside more than 800 logs, all sourced from Missouri-native species such as walnut, cherry, oak, and sassafras. Beyond milling customer-supplied logs, the team produces custom furniture and accessories—tables, paddles, benches, charcuterie boards, bartops, and mantel pieces—while also selling dimensional lumber to contractors, builders, and DIY enthusiasts.

Customers range from professional contractors and builders seeking sustainable Missouri hardwood to hobbyists commissioning one-off pieces. The business also serves woodworkers who bring their own logs for custom milling, offering a full chain from raw log to finished slab or product.

Wayne describes himself as a “Tree Whisperer,” aiming to let each piece of wood “speak for itself” by revealing its unique grain and character. The venture began as a retirement pursuit after decades at Boeing, driven by a desire to honor the natural beauty of local timber rather than chase volume metrics.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sawmilling", "Custom woodworking", "Milling services", "Live edge slab production", "Lumber sales", "Custom furniture fabrication"], "industries": ["Construction", "Renovation", "Woodworking", "DIY", "Custom furniture", "Contractors", "Builders"], "materials": ["Walnut", "Cherry", "Oak", "Sassafras", "Missouri native hardwoods"], "equipment": ["Two sawmills"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Two sawmills on site for custom milling", "Over 50,000 board feet of live-edge slabs in stock", "Works with customer-supplied logs", "All lumber sourced from Missouri-native species", "Veteran-owned and operated"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1994 by Wayne (Vietnam veteran, former Boeing tech rep) -> /about-us", "Location: 3540 North Highway 94, St. Charles, MO 63301 -> /", "Two sawmills on site -> /", "Inventory: over 50,000 board feet of slabs, 800+ logs -> /", "Wood species: Walnut, Cherry, Oak, Sassafras, all Missouri native -> /", "Services: custom milling, custom woodworking, lumber sales, live edge slabs -> /", "Products: tables, paddles, benches, charcuterie boards, bartops, mantel pieces -> /", "Customer types: contractors, builders, DIY enthusiasts, woodworkers with own logs -> /", "Veteran-owned (Wayne served 4 years in Vietnam) -> /about-us", "Company philosophy: ''Tree Whisperer'', let wood speak for itself -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We specialize in custom woodworking and sawmilling.", "founded_year": "1994", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='saw-logs-to-lumber' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Schaumburg Specialties operates from Schaumburg, Illinois, producing custom metal racks and carts for food production and industrial applications. The company does not publicly disclose its founding year, ownership structure, or founder names.

The company manufactures oven racks, bakery carts, processing tables, dough troughs, donut racks, speed racks, pan racks, lug racks, sheet pans, wire screens, and nesting racks under the SHOPCraft, KWIKCraft, and AGRICraft product lines. Its capabilities include custom metal fabrication, welded construction, design and engineering, bulk product development, and maintenance and equipment servicing. All products are built using all-welded construction with top-of-the-line materials such as 18-gauge aluminum and stainless steel, and carry a lifetime guarantee.

Schaumburg Specialties serves industrial bakeries, donut production lines, airline catering commissaries, prepared meal facilities, meat and seafood processors, pet food manufacturers, and agriculture and indoor farming operations. Customer references include David''s Burgers, Bimbo, Udi''s (Pinnacle Foods), Illinois State University, Carolina CPL Co-Op, and businesses in Appleton, WI; Elk Grove, IL; and Chapel Hill, NC.

